      "title": "H3 Ripple · Models & setup",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# H3 Ripple — Model downloads\n\nInstall [ComfyUI-WepeNerd](https://github.com/WepeNerd/ComfyUI-WepeNerd) and use a current ComfyUI version. Download the five files below; folders are relative to your ComfyUI directory.\n\n### H3 FL2VA diffusion model · [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/diffusion_models/minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n\n`minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/diffusion_models/`.\n\n### H3 Turbo 4-step LoRA · [Download](https://huggingface.co/lightx2v/Minimax-h3-Turbo/resolve/main/minimax_h3_fl2v_turbo_4step_v1.3_768p_comfyui_bf16.safetensors)\n\n`minimax_h3_fl2v_turbo_4step_v1.3_768p_comfyui_bf16.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/loras/H3/`.\n\n### H3 Ripple LoRA · [Model page](https://huggingface.co/WepeNerd/H3_Ripple)\n\n`minimax_H3_Ripple-v1.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/loras/H3/`.\n\n### H3 text encoder · [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors)\n\n`qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/text_encoders/`.\n\n### H3 video VAE · [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors)\n\n`minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/vae/`.\n\n### Workflow settings\n\nThe Turbo LoRA is enabled: **4 steps · Euler · simple · CFG 1**. Both LoRA strengths are **1.0**. The CLIP loader type is **minimax**. Refresh the model lists or restart ComfyUI after copying the files, then select them in the loaders.\n\nThis workflow expects the Ripple filename shown above. If the published download has a different name, select that file in the Ripple LoRA loader.\n\n### Using the workflow\n\nChoose your video and shot in Ripple Clip. Download the marked frames, edit them externally, and upload each edit to its matching card. Ripple Output is enabled and saves the shot and comparison. Source audio is reused; an audio VAE and a separate image-editing model are not needed for this workflow."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# H3 Ripple — Model downloads\n\nInstall [ComfyUI-WepeNerd](https://github.com/WepeNerd/ComfyUI-WepeNerd) and use a current ComfyUI version. Download the five files below; folders are relative to your ComfyUI directory.\n\n### H3 FL2VA diffusion model · [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/diffusion_models/minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n\n`minimax_h3_fl2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/diffusion_models/`.\n\n### H3 Turbo 4-step LoRA · [Download](https://huggingface.co/lightx2v/Minimax-h3-Turbo/resolve/main/minimax_h3_fl2v_turbo_4step_v1.3_768p_comfyui_bf16.safetensors)\n\n`minimax_h3_fl2v_turbo_4step_v1.3_768p_comfyui_bf16.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/loras/H3/`.\n\n### H3 Ripple LoRA · [Model page](https://huggingface.co/WepeNerd/H3_Ripple)\n\n`minimax_H3_Ripple-v1.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/loras/H3/`.\n\n### H3 text encoder · [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors)\n\n`qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/text_encoders/`.\n\n### H3 video VAE · [Download](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3/resolve/main/vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors)\n\n`minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors`\n\nSave in `models/vae/`.\n\n### Workflow settings\n\nThe Turbo LoRA is enabled: **4 steps · Euler · simple · CFG 1**. Both LoRA strengths are **1.0**. The CLIP loader type is **minimax**. Refresh the model lists or restart ComfyUI after copying the files, then select them in the loaders.\n\nThis workflow expects the Ripple filename shown above. If the published download has a different name, select that file in the Ripple LoRA loader.\n\n### Using the workflow\n\nChoose your video and shot in Ripple Clip. Download the marked frames, edit them externally, and upload each edit to its matching card. Ripple Output is enabled and saves the shot and comparison. Source audio is reused; an audio VAE and a separate image-editing model are not needed for this workflow."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
